      "message": "The actual problem is that when you are passing a subclass of BpfRingbufBase via the BpfRingbufBase interface and subsequently destroy the object, only the destructor for BpfRingbufBase is called, *not* the entire destructor chain. Having a virtual destructor obviously solves that, because no matter the type, the vtable will always point to the \"bottom\"-most destructor. But yes, unless you have a custom destructor or class members, it technically doesn\u0027t matter.",
